1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,640
Frieren.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:06,730
You must find Aureole
and speak with Himmel.

3
00:00:08,450 --> 00:00:11,260
"On the northernmost end of the continent..."

4
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:15,900
<i>I arrived at the place the people
of this world call heaven:</i>

5
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:19,820
<i>Aureole, the land where souls rest.</i>

6
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:23,610
<i>Many souls gather there,</i>

7
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:27,330
<i>and I spoke with friends
who once fought alongside me.</i>

8
00:00:30,710 --> 00:00:32,160
Sorry to ask this of you.

9
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,490
It'll be a long journey.

10
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:37,950
It took us ten years.

11
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:41,360
I see.

12
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:46,100
We'll be following the same path Mr. Himmel's
party took to the Demon King's castle.

13
00:00:56,990 --> 00:00:58,160
You're right.

14
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:01,260
It'll be a mere ten-year adventure.

15
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,510
One one-hundredth, huh?

16
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:11,040
Frieren, you're not going
to stay in the royal capital?

17
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,130
I'm going to keep traveling.

18
00:01:13,130 --> 00:01:14,540
Alone?

19
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:16,200
It'll be nice and easy.

20
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:19,300
You're not going to take on an apprentice?

21
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:22,280
Traveling is better when you
have someone to talk to.

22
00:01:22,620 --> 00:01:24,860
It's a waste of time.

23
00:01:24,860 --> 00:01:27,780
Even if I taught them,
they'd die in no time.

24
00:01:30,310 --> 00:01:34,680
Frieren, that's not how relationships work.

25
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,960
Yes, it is.

26
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:42,050
My adventure with you wasn't even
one one-hundredth of my life.

27
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:45,600
I might've said something like that.

28
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,100
It's funny, isn't it?

29
00:01:49,550 --> 00:01:50,730
What is?

30
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:56,010
That one one-hundredth changed you.

31
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,500
Well, I'll see you later.

32
00:02:10,150 --> 00:02:12,120
See you again.

33
00:02:19,770 --> 00:02:22,670
It's been half my life, you know.

34
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:26,630
The time I've spent with you.

35
00:02:28,850 --> 00:02:31,410
It's going to be even more
than that from now on.

36
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:36,070
<i>Like a fairy tale</i>

37
00:02:36,070 --> 00:02:38,480
<i>It's a sign the story has reached its end</i>

38
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:41,400
<i>Like a single passage taken from</i>

39
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,020
<i>A journey that was too long</i>

40
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:45,390
<i>Of the evil that once cast a shadow</i>

41
00:02:45,390 --> 00:02:47,720
<i>Across this land</i>

42
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:50,040
<i>And the memories of the short journey</i>

43
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:52,490
<i>With the hero who defeated it</i>

44
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:04,800
<i>The story ends</i>

45
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:07,310
<i>And the hero goes to sleep</i>

46
00:03:07,310 --> 00:03:10,150
<i>Leaving this land with</i>

47
00:03:10,150 --> 00:03:11,800
<i>Days of peace and quiet</i>

48
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:14,310
<i>The passage of time heartlessly</i>

49
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:16,490
<i>Makes people forget</i>

50
00:03:16,490 --> 00:03:19,270
<i>Even the tracks left behind by his life</i>

51
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:21,060
<i>Begin to rust</i>

52
00:03:21,060 --> 00:03:22,900
<i>Just the same</i>

53
00:03:22,900 --> 00:03:25,190
<i>Your words and wishes and courage</i>

54
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:28,530
<i>Are still inside of me</i>

55
00:03:28,530 --> 00:03:30,400
<i>And they live on</i>

56
00:03:31,230 --> 00:03:32,950
<i>We chose the same path</i>

57
00:03:32,950 --> 00:03:35,100
<i>That's all it was supposed to be</i>

58
00:03:35,100 --> 00:03:36,630
<i>Why is it that at some point</i>

59
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:40,880
<i>I wanted to understand the reason for</i>

60
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:42,260
<i>The tears that fall down my cheeks</i>

61
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:43,340
<i>Even now</i>

62
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:45,720
<i>If I retrace the journey we walked together</i>

63
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:49,270
<i>Even though you're not there</i>

64
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:50,920
<i>I know I'll be able to find it</i>

65
00:04:07,170 --> 00:04:09,250
Listen to me, Fern.

66
00:04:09,670 --> 00:04:15,090
From now, you must listen carefully to what
Frieren tells you and be a good girl,

67
00:04:15,850 --> 00:04:17,250
or else...

68
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,760
Or else what?

69
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:22,530
I'll haunt you after I'm dead.

70
00:04:26,300 --> 00:04:31,610
Mr. Heiter, do you mean that if I'm a bad
girl, you'll come see me after you die?

71
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:40,980
You've grown into a clever girl.
Who taught you to act like that?

72
00:04:42,170 --> 00:04:43,840
I take it back.

73
00:04:45,770 --> 00:04:52,050
If you're a good girl, then I might
be willing to visit you sometimes.

74
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:59,410
We're almost at the village.

75
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:03,170
I see.

76
00:05:04,130 --> 00:05:05,020
What?

77
00:05:05,580 --> 00:05:07,380
Nothing.

78
00:05:26,250 --> 00:05:29,400
You're heading to the mountain pass, right?

79
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:31,800
I wouldn't if I were you.

80
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:34,650
A bunch of people have gone missing.

81
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:36,910
Was it monsters?

82
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:40,230
Taken by ghosts, or so the rumors say.

83
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:42,450
Some people have seen them
with their own eyes.

84
00:05:42,450 --> 00:05:44,130
Could be the undead.

85
00:05:44,130 --> 00:05:46,670
Do you know what the ghosts look like?

86
00:05:46,670 --> 00:05:48,630
I'm afraid not.

87
00:05:48,630 --> 00:05:51,500
But if you're curious,
why not ask them yourselves?

88
00:06:02,290 --> 00:06:03,780
To summarize,

89
00:06:04,520 --> 00:06:10,550
people saw the ghosts of dead family and
acquaintances as they appeared in life.

90
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:14,780
Some witnesses claimed the
ghosts spoke to them.

91
00:06:15,870 --> 00:06:18,980
This isn't the work of the undead.

92
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:20,510
It's not?

93
00:06:23,230 --> 00:06:27,400
The undead are corpses controlled by magic,

94
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,970
like zombies or skeletons.

95
00:06:31,510 --> 00:06:34,840
But these ghosts appeared
as they did in life.

96
00:06:35,410 --> 00:06:37,390
A reanimated corpse wouldn't look like that.

97
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:42,100
This is the work of a completely
different type of monster.

98
00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:46,360
You seem to have some inkling
of what it might be.

99
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:51,540
It's a nasty one. We'd best
be careful to avoid it.

100
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:56,840
We'll leave first thing in the morning.

101
00:06:57,630 --> 00:07:01,630
Ms. Frieren, the villagers need help.

102
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:04,960
You sound like Himmel and the others.

103
00:07:05,350 --> 00:07:08,730
Unlike you, I'm a good girl.

104
00:07:09,130 --> 00:07:12,740
If you want to help, then I suppose we can.

105
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:16,300
We'll be traveling through the
mountain pass either way.

106
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:34,470
This is where the villagers have
been disappearing recently.

107
00:07:35,800 --> 00:07:40,130
At least there are plenty of clues.

108
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:43,770
There are signs of magic use here.

109
00:07:44,300 --> 00:07:47,370
Yes. What kind of magic do you think it was?

110
00:07:48,090 --> 00:07:49,720
Illusion magic.

111
00:07:50,760 --> 00:07:54,380
I read in a book on magical ecology
that there's a monster

112
00:07:54,850 --> 00:07:57,660
that uses illusions to lure prey.

113
00:07:58,230 --> 00:07:59,640
The Einsam.

114
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:03,180
Even among monsters of its type,

115
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:07,530
it's an especially crafty and greedy
monster that consumes only humans.

116
00:08:08,510 --> 00:08:11,650
It shows people phantoms
of the dead to lure them in.

117
00:08:12,250 --> 00:08:14,650
Does that really work?

118
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:18,870
They're illusions of people very dear to them.

119
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:26,670
But the Einsam's illusions
aren't a threat to mages.

120
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:32,540
They're easily dispersed by high-density
mana such as offensive magic.

121
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:35,930
So we just need to shoot
the phantoms of the dead.

122
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:39,380
Could you?

123
00:08:40,670 --> 00:08:41,970
Of course.

124
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:44,890
After all, I know they're fake.

125
00:08:45,370 --> 00:08:49,150
I shot a phantom of my master
begging for her life.

126
00:08:50,680 --> 00:08:54,150
But I was used to hearing her
beg for her life,

127
00:08:54,150 --> 00:08:57,220
so I didn't feel particularly
guilty about it.

128
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:00,790
Either way, it doesn't feel good.

129
00:09:01,180 --> 00:09:04,680
What does it mean that you were accustomed
to hearing her beg for her life?

130
00:09:10,530 --> 00:09:12,510
It's gotten misty.

131
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:14,700
We're close.

132
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:18,970
If you see a phantom,
don't hesitate to shoot it.

133
00:09:24,050 --> 00:09:25,030
Fern.

134
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:33,990
<i>There it is. A phantom of the dead.</i>

135
00:09:35,850 --> 00:09:37,230
<i>I'm calm.</i>

136
00:09:38,610 --> 00:09:39,730
<i>I can shoot it.</i>

137
00:09:41,710 --> 00:09:45,620
You've become quite the mage.

138
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:53,500
I decided to pay you a visit
because you've been a good girl.

139
00:09:56,770 --> 00:09:57,830
<i>My memories...</i>

140
00:09:57,830 --> 00:10:01,530
You were right to choose the path of a mage.

141
00:10:01,530 --> 00:10:04,950
You've always loved magic.

142
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:07,000
<i>It's using my memories against me.</i>

143
00:10:04,950 --> 00:10:10,400
You were so happy when
I gave you that staff.

144
00:10:07,740 --> 00:10:09,730
<i>How cruel.</i>

145
00:10:10,370 --> 00:10:12,970
<i>One of my most cherished memories...</i>

146
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:12,250
You slept with it every night.

147
00:10:15,190 --> 00:10:16,170
Fern.

148
00:10:19,750 --> 00:10:21,140
No, huh?

149
00:10:28,980 --> 00:10:31,170
So it's Himmel this time.

150
00:10:31,770 --> 00:10:35,540
I assumed it'd be my master again.

151
00:10:36,790 --> 00:10:40,170
Does this mean I've changed?

152
00:10:43,680 --> 00:10:46,690
Frieren, shoot me.

153
00:10:47,740 --> 00:10:51,220
Right. That's what Himmel would say.

154
00:11:13,460 --> 00:11:16,080
Now the mountain pass is safe again.

155
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:18,530
Ms. Frieren...

156
00:11:19,270 --> 00:11:21,960
That was a phantom of Mr. Heiter.

157
00:11:22,500 --> 00:11:23,950
An impostor.

158
00:11:23,950 --> 00:11:25,130
Yes.

159
00:11:28,780 --> 00:11:31,150
Let's go see the real Heiter now.

160
00:11:32,220 --> 00:11:35,360
After all, we're trying to reach Aureole.

161
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,150
You're right.

162
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:51,240
That's a dragon?

163
00:11:52,810 --> 00:11:54,690
I've never seen one before.

164
00:11:55,770 --> 00:11:57,090
Look at its nest.

165
00:11:58,610 --> 00:12:00,410
See that grimoire?

166
00:12:00,930 --> 00:12:03,560
It's one I've been looking for.

167
00:12:03,560 --> 00:12:05,690
You do love your grimoires.

168
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:08,160
But what's it doing there?

169
00:12:08,740 --> 00:12:12,940
Dragons use objects infused
with magic to build their nests.

170
00:12:13,950 --> 00:12:15,350
That's a solar dragon.

171
00:12:16,030 --> 00:12:18,930
It's eaten numerous adventurers.

172
00:12:19,410 --> 00:12:22,400
Either way, we should probably take it out.

173
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:26,180
Be careful you don't hit the nest.

174
00:12:26,180 --> 00:12:26,980
Got it.

175
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:43,990
Ms. Frieren, that didn't do anything.

176
00:12:43,990 --> 00:12:46,300
Figures. Dragons really are tough.

177
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:48,380
We have no choice, then. Let's run.

178
00:13:07,160 --> 00:13:09,170
We finally lost it.

179
00:13:09,650 --> 00:13:11,680
It's a quick flyer, too.

180
00:13:11,680 --> 00:13:13,950
I doubt we can beat it in an aerial battle.

181
00:13:13,950 --> 00:13:18,400
I... I thought I was going to die.

182
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:19,700
Let's head back.

183
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:23,650
If we repeat that process enough times,
we'll beat it eventually.

184
00:13:28,250 --> 00:13:29,370
Of course.

185
00:13:29,950 --> 00:13:34,140
Mages don't play tag with dragons.

186
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,980
I guess we'll just have
to take on a companion.

187
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:45,750
A front-liner?

188
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:48,610
Yeah. You're searching
for someone, aren't you?

189
00:13:48,940 --> 00:13:54,020
There's a warrior named Stark
in a village near Riegel Canyon.

190
00:13:54,020 --> 00:13:57,620
Pick him up on your way
into the northern lands.

191
00:13:57,620 --> 00:13:59,710
He's my apprentice.

192
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:03,370
Huh. Is he a good warrior?

193
00:14:14,980 --> 00:14:18,770
It's so peaceful, it's hard to
believe there's a dragon nearby.

194
00:14:18,770 --> 00:14:20,100
You're right.

195
00:14:22,140 --> 00:14:27,670
Ms. Frieren, what kind of magic
does that grimoire contain?

196
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:30,410
A spell that lets you see through clothes.

197
00:14:33,490 --> 00:14:37,790
You really do collect a lot of odd spells.

198
00:14:37,790 --> 00:14:39,450
It's my hobby, after all.

199
00:14:40,210 --> 00:14:42,460
But it's practical, too.

200
00:14:42,910 --> 00:14:47,730
Depending on what you consider clothes,
it can reveal hidden weapons—

201
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:50,380
Travelers, may I have a moment of your time?

202
00:14:51,370 --> 00:14:54,300
Mr. Stark would like to meet you.

203
00:14:54,990 --> 00:14:57,210
Well, that saves us having to look for him.

204
00:15:01,270 --> 00:15:07,470
Three years ago, that dragon
attacked the village.

205
00:15:14,650 --> 00:15:19,070
That's when Mr. Stark appeared.

206
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:23,340
He stood his ground in front of that dragon.

207
00:15:23,340 --> 00:15:28,210
After a long standoff, the dragon left.

208
00:15:28,210 --> 00:15:32,470
Since then, because he's stayed here,

209
00:15:32,470 --> 00:15:37,850
the dragon hasn't attacked,
and we've lived in peace.

210
00:15:39,300 --> 00:15:44,250
Then perhaps we could defeat
the dragon with Mr. Stark's help.

211
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:46,110
I hope you're right.

212
00:15:48,430 --> 00:15:51,980
Do you think I can become
a powerful warrior like you?

213
00:15:51,980 --> 00:15:53,120
Sure you can.

214
00:15:53,560 --> 00:15:56,360
But a warrior's job is hardly a noble one.

215
00:15:58,680 --> 00:16:00,760
Grandma!

216
00:16:08,530 --> 00:16:11,220
So you're the ones who
messed with the dragon.

217
00:16:11,910 --> 00:16:15,720
Don't get it too worked up.
You'll put the village in danger.

218
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:20,470
Dragons are far more terrifying
than you think they are.

219
00:16:22,350 --> 00:16:25,820
I got this scar on my forehead
fighting a shadow dragon—

220
00:16:25,820 --> 00:16:27,970
It's not that serious an injury.

221
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,670
Did my master put you up to this?

222
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:33,740
Who are you?

223
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:36,750
Frieren the Mage.

224
00:16:39,490 --> 00:16:41,860
Grandma, could you give us some privacy?

225
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:46,480
It's all right.
They're acquaintances of my master.

226
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:54,840
My master must be furious.

227
00:16:55,490 --> 00:16:57,640
I left him without so much as a word.

228
00:16:58,270 --> 00:17:01,920
Stark, why haven't you defeated the dragon?

229
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:04,440
You have no reason to remain in this village.

230
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:07,950
Why don't you tell me what you want first?

231
00:17:08,470 --> 00:17:11,610
If you're here to send me back
to my master, then forget it.

232
00:17:12,730 --> 00:17:16,300
We want you to join us as our front-liner,

233
00:17:16,300 --> 00:17:20,030
though before that, we'd appreciate
your help in defeating the solar dragon.

234
00:17:20,470 --> 00:17:23,330
I want the grimoire in its nest.

235
00:17:23,330 --> 00:17:24,170
Why?

236
00:17:24,620 --> 00:17:27,670
It's just a hobby. No particular reason.

237
00:17:28,040 --> 00:17:30,420
We're talking about a solar dragon here.

238
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:32,920
It's not something you fight
for no particular reason.

239
00:17:41,400 --> 00:17:42,830
Wow!

240
00:17:44,230 --> 00:17:45,690
You're right.

241
00:17:46,090 --> 00:17:49,730
There was once an idiot who
complimented the spells I collected.

242
00:17:50,460 --> 00:17:52,320
Is that enough of a reason for you?

243
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:56,010
Complimented you, huh?

244
00:17:58,660 --> 00:17:59,960
That's ridiculous.

245
00:17:59,960 --> 00:18:00,980
Right?

246
00:18:01,930 --> 00:18:04,360
I don't mind joining your party.

247
00:18:05,200 --> 00:18:07,660
My master told you to take
me with you, didn't he?

248
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:12,070
But I need the solar
dragon dealt with first.

249
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:15,200
Honestly, I've had trouble
defeating it alone.

250
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:19,710
Frieren, you can defeat it, can't you?

251
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:23,730
If you can keep it busy
for thirty seconds, certainly.

252
00:18:24,340 --> 00:18:28,500
I see. Thirty seconds, huh?

253
00:18:30,340 --> 00:18:33,060
Do I really have to do that?

254
00:18:33,060 --> 00:18:35,470
What is he talking about?

255
00:18:35,910 --> 00:18:38,060
I thought so.

256
00:18:38,660 --> 00:18:41,980
Stark, how much experience
do you have fighting monsters?

257
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:43,730
Zero!

258
00:18:43,730 --> 00:18:46,500
Help me, Frieren!

259
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:49,740
I confronted the dragon at first.

260
00:18:50,010 --> 00:18:53,760
But I was so scared,
I couldn't move a muscle!

261
00:18:54,070 --> 00:18:58,520
It slices through houses
like they're vegetables!

262
00:18:58,520 --> 00:19:01,770
A human doesn't stand a chance against it!

263
00:19:02,990 --> 00:19:05,990
I figured it spared me on a whim, but then...

264
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:13,160
For some reason the dragon stopped attacking
the village, and I was treated like a hero.

265
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:16,390
And the villagers are such nice people!

266
00:19:16,390 --> 00:19:18,700
You're still young. Get plenty to eat.

267
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:21,780
Stark, show me your new killer move!

268
00:19:22,050 --> 00:19:25,900
I couldn't leave if I wanted to.

269
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:30,530
Ms. Frieren, this one is no good.
Let's find someone else.

270
00:19:30,530 --> 00:19:33,240
Please don't abandon me!

271
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:38,040
No, he can fight the dragon. I know he can.

272
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:41,230
He'll need more than just encouragement...

273
00:20:02,190 --> 00:20:05,500
Stark, you have until tomorrow morning.

274
00:20:06,360 --> 00:20:07,960
Think carefully.

275
00:20:08,310 --> 00:20:11,460
I know you realize
you can't keep this up.

276
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:28,180
You met Mr. Stark?

277
00:20:28,540 --> 00:20:30,540
He's a nice young man, isn't he?

278
00:20:30,540 --> 00:20:35,190
He seems to really enjoy our cooking.

279
00:20:36,050 --> 00:20:38,310
People really love Mr. Stark.

280
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:42,310
Well, he seems like a kind person.

281
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:44,190
Kind?

282
00:20:45,040 --> 00:20:47,640
He only seemed cowardly to me.

283
00:20:48,210 --> 00:20:50,840
I won't deny the cowardly part.

284
00:20:50,840 --> 00:20:54,210
But in your first battle against monsters...

285
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:57,840
Okay, okay. I'll forget about that.

286
00:21:01,130 --> 00:21:05,850
Honestly, you were so meek
and cute when you were little.

287
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:11,280
By the way, why doesn't the
dragon attack this village?

288
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:15,840
Who knows? It could be
mere whimsy, or perhaps...

289
00:21:18,560 --> 00:21:20,100
What's that sound?

290
00:21:20,540 --> 00:21:22,100
Stark, probably.

291
00:21:23,660 --> 00:21:25,600
If you're curious, why not check on him?

292
00:21:26,050 --> 00:21:27,720
I'm going to bed.

293
00:21:44,990 --> 00:21:47,850
Huh. Is he a good warrior?

294
00:21:50,530 --> 00:21:58,780
He was the only one who ran when monsters
attacked his hometown. A coward.

295
00:22:00,550 --> 00:22:02,170
He's like me.

296
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:08,240
So I taught him everything I knew.

297
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:13,240
Now he's someone who can fight for another.

298
00:22:14,010 --> 00:22:17,130
I see. He's a good warrior, then.

299
00:22:38,150 --> 00:22:41,470
So this fissure was left by your training.

300
00:22:49,980 --> 00:22:52,520
<i>And you alright</i>

301
00:22:53,050 --> 00:22:55,040
<i>Can you hear me</i>

302
00:22:55,830 --> 00:23:01,940
<i>Trailing along deserted train tracks</i>

303
00:23:01,940 --> 00:23:04,270
<i>Crying excessively</i>

304
00:23:04,830 --> 00:23:07,440
<i>Wanting you to smile</i>

305
00:23:07,440 --> 00:23:13,480
<i>I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh</i>

306
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:17,170
<i>There's something I'd like to tell you</i>

307
00:23:17,170 --> 00:23:19,960
<i>With words more precious than a goodbye</i>

308
00:23:19,960 --> 00:23:25,630
<i>Unremarkable yet special</i>

309
00:23:25,630 --> 00:23:29,150
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

310
00:23:29,150 --> 00:23:32,200
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

311
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:36,960
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

312
00:23:36,960 --> 00:23:43,060
<i>So, if I were to be born again</i>

313
00:23:43,060 --> 00:23:48,880
<i>I would surely choose this place once more</i>

314
00:23:48,880 --> 00:23:54,890
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

315
00:23:54,890 --> 00:24:00,650
<i>I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present</i>

316
00:24:00,650 --> 00:24:03,600
<i>Even if no promises were made</i>

317
00:24:03,600 --> 00:24:06,520
<i>Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness</i>

318
00:24:06,520 --> 00:24:12,720
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

319
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:15,360
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby</i>

320
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:19,280
<i>for you to come back home</i>

321
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:22,280
The passage of time is cruel.

322
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:22,000
That old hag...

323
00:24:21,170 --> 00:24:23,120
Isn't that a bit dangerous?

324
00:24:21,930 --> 00:24:24,370
Don't cause any trouble in this town.

325
00:24:23,350 --> 00:24:25,500
He must've been disappointed in me.

326
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:26,020
We parted in anger.

327
00:24:25,020 --> 00:24:26,750
His hands are trembling.

328
00:24:25,890 --> 00:24:27,890
They even tremble the same way.

329
00:24:27,890 --> 00:24:30,020
I'm Stark, the hero of this village.
